  "nl_text": "This schema is for a database that stores information about a stock exchange, including companies, brokers, traders, and transactions. The database is called schemabench_0160 and it has eight tables.\nThe first table, company_info, stores information about the companies that are traded on the exchange. It has the following columns: company_id (primary key), company_name, streetNo, city, c_state, zipcode, and established_date.\nThe second table, exchange, stores information about the exchange itself. It has the following columns: exchange_id (primary key), exchange_name.\nThe third table, broker_info, stores information about the brokers who work on the exchange. It has the following columns: broker_id (primary key), broker_fname, broker_lname, broker_contact, broker_streetno, broker_streetname, broker_city, broker_state, and broker_zip.\nThe fourth table, trader_info, stores information about the traders who participate in the exchange. It has the following columns: trader_id (primary key), trader_fname, trader_lname, account_no, trader_contact, trader_streetno, trader_streetname, trader_city, trader_state, and trader_zip.\nThe fifth table, Account_info, stores information about the accounts that traders use to buy and sell stocks. It has the following columns: account_id (primary key), cash, security, trader_id (foreign key), broker_id (foreign key).\nThe sixth table, broker_exchange_deals, stores information about the deals that brokers make on behalf of traders. It has the following columns: id (primary key), fees_given, broker_id (foreign key), exchange_id (foreign key).\nThe seventh table, stock_info, stores information about the stocks that are traded on the exchange. It has the following columns: stock_id (primary key), stock_name, shares_no, stock_symbol, stock_launchDate, s_price, company_id (foreign key), trade_exchange_id (foreign key).\nThe eighth and final table, transaction_info, stores information about the transactions that take place on the exchange. It has the following columns: order_id (primary key), T_Price, No_Of_Shares, brokeragepaidby_seller, brokeragepaidby_buyer, id (foreign key), stock_id (foreign key), broker_id (foreign key), exchange_id (foreign key), trader_id (foreign key), account_id (foreign key).\nIn summary, this schema is a comprehensive database that stores information about a stock exchange, including companies, brokers, traders, and transactions. It has eight tables, each with its own set of columns, and each table has its own unique purpose in storing and organizing the data.",
  "gold_question": "Stock Trading System\n\n 1) Background / Context\nThe Stock Trading System is an automated platform designed to manage the trading of stocks for publicly traded companies. The system simplifies search, purchase, and management of stock holdings through individual user portfolios.\n\n 2) Objectives\n- Facilitate efficient trading of stocks.\n- Streamline the management of user portfolios.\n- Ensure secure and accurate processing of transactions across multiple exchanges.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Traders: Individuals who own and trade stocks through brokerages.\n- Brokers: Entities that facilitate stock trades between traders and exchanges.\n- Stock Exchanges: Platforms where stocks are listed and traded.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- Company Management: \n  - Manage company information, including name, headquarters address, and established date.\n  - Each public company is associated with a unique stock.\n\n- Stock Trading:\n  - Each stock is identified by a unique stock code and possible to be traded on up to 9 exchanges.\n  - Stocks are associated with symbols unique to each exchange.\n  - Record last trading price and daily volume per symbol.\n\n- Trader and Account Management:\n  - Traders have unique IDs and may own multiple accounts.\n  - Accounts hold securities and cash, and are linked to specific brokers.\n\n- Broker Management:\n  - Brokers manage trades and pay exchange fees.\n  - Manage broker information, including contact details and state.\n\n- Transaction Management:\n  - Allow traders to place orders and process through brokerages.\n  - Each transaction records number of shares, price, commissions, and a timestamp.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Performance: Efficient handling of high-volume transactions.\n- Security: Ensure secure handling of user data and trading executions.\n- Scalability: Support a growing number of traders and stock exchanges.\n- Reliability: Accurate record-keeping and transaction processing are crucial.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0160.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0160\nCREATE TABLE `company_info` (\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `company_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `streetNo` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `c_state` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `zipcode` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `established_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`company_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `exchange` (\n  `exchange_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `exchange_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`exchange_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `broker_info` (\n  `broker_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `broker_fname` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `broker_lname` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `broker_contact` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `broker_streetno` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `broker_streetname` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `broker_city` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `broker_state` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `broker_zip` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`broker_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `trader_info` (\n  `trader_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `trader_fname` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `trader_lname` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `account_no` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `trader_contact` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `trader_streetno` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `trader_streetname` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `trader_city` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `trader_state` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `trader_zip` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`trader_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `account_info` (\n  `account_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `cash` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `security` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `trader_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `broker_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`account_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `account_info_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`trader_id`) REFERENCES `trader_info` (`trader_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `account_info_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`broker_id`) REFERENCES `broker_info` (`broker_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `broker_exchange_deals` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `fees_given` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `broker_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `exchange_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `broker_exchange_deals_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`broker_id`) REFERENCES `broker_info` (`broker_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `broker_exchange_deals_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`exchange_id`) REFERENCES `exchange` (`exchange_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stock_info` (\n  `stock_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stock_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `shares_no` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stock_symbol` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `stock_launchDate` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `s_price` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `trade_exchange_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`stock_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `stock_info_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`company_id`) REFERENCES `company_info` (`company_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `stock_info_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`trade_exchange_id`) REFERENCES `exchange` (`exchange_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `transaction_info` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `T_Price` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `No_Of_Shares` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `brokeragepaidby_seller` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `brokeragepaidby_buyer` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stock_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `broker_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `exchange_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `trader_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `account_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_info_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`id`) REFERENCES `broker_exchange_deals` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_info_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`stock_id`) REFERENCES `stock_info` (`stock_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_info_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`broker_id`) REFERENCES `broker_info` (`broker_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_info_ibfk_4` FOREIGN KEY (`exchange_id`) REFERENCES `exchange` (`exchange_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_info_ibfk_5` FOREIGN KEY (`trader_id`) REFERENCES `trader_info` (`trader_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_info_ibfk_6` FOREIGN KEY (`account_id`) REFERENCES `account_info` (`account_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
